API-P4 completed: rich extension tool results now cross the production Host-to-Rust-to-sequential/parallel execution path. The generated extension contract owns file purposes and the 16-block, 8-file, 20 MiB/result and 64 MiB/parallel-batch limits; richToolResults is advertised only with the complete path.

Security decisions: the Host snapshots each result/array/block field once into frozen null-prototype data, measures the escaped JSON-RPC message, and keeps the snapshot as a proven production dependency from loader.mjs. Rust reuses verified_file_read, open_regular_single_link, attachment_access_identity, file_signature and the existing HMAC grant authority. File identity is checked around bounded reads; cancellation and replacements fail closed; workspace keys never reach Node/frontend. Extension resources are deferred, revalidated against current session/trust/source/declaration/catalog state, and expose only qualified resource identity plus catalog fingerprint.

Parallel correctness: one coordinator budget is applied after collecting all read/write chunks, in original result order. Three 20 MiB results are admitted and only the fourth fails. Ordinary neighbors survive cancellation/key failures. Sequential and parallel outcomes retain ephemeral bytes with real tool_call_index and tool_call_id; diagnostics complete once after artifact resolution. Metadata and bytes remain separate; no base64 or internal extension resource path is serialized.

Root review corrections: moved resolution after the complete read/write batch; preserved non-pending neighbors on cancellation; added cancellation during a real chunked read, file replacement during read, resource authority-change tests, and read-write-read attribution coverage; bounded derived Unicode filenames; removed Array.prototype dispatch for purpose checks; removed a duplicated test-only resolver so tests exercise the production coordinator.

